Main document that executes the production of a finished product or sub-assembly based on a Bill of Materials (BOM), managing the full lifecycle from planning to completion.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Launch production orders from sales orders, forecasts, or manually
Consume raw materials and produce finished goods
Split production into work orders per operation
Track production progress, scrap, and by-products
Automatic reservation and replenishment of components
Costing of production (real vs standard)
Mass production, rework, and unplanned orders

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent + mail.thread + activity.mixin)
Key Fields:
name (sequenced), product_id / product_tmpl_id
bom_id → mrp.bom, product_qty, qty_produced, qty_producing
state (draft/confirmed/planned/progress/done/cancel)
date_planned_start, date_planned_finished, date_deadline
One2many: move_raw_ids (component consumption), move_finished_ids, workorder_ids
lot_producing_id, origin (sales order link)

Critical Hooks: action_confirm, button_mark_done, _generate_workorders, action_assign, _compute_cost, do_unreserve
Security: mrp.group_mrp_manager + company + warehouse rules

RAG Routing Keywords:
manufacturing order, production order, MO, mrp.production, work order, produce, manufacturing execution, production planning, BOM production, finished goods production, production confirmation, production done, workcenter production, planned production, in progress, to produce, pending manufacturing order, late production, cancelled MO, production status, manufacturing order state
Related Models (most joined):

mrp.bom & mrp.bom.line
mrp.workorder (child operations)
stock.move (raw & finished moves)
product.product
sale.order (via origin)
mrp.workcenter
stock.warehouse / stock.location

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
mrp.production is Odoo’s core Manufacturing Order model that executes production using a BOM, with product_id, product_qty, state, planned dates, and links to move_raw_ids, move_finished_ids, and workorder_ids. It drives component reservation & consumption, work order generation, finished goods receipt, production costing, and full integration between Manufacturing, Inventory, and Sales modules.